 "meta": {
  "version": "1.0",
  "units": "metres",
  "frame": "each model in its own frame: z up, front -y. The pile: origin on the ground at its middle; the clump: origin at the middle of the bale (the grip). In trash.blend the piles stand in a row and each clump 2 m in front of its pile, on the ground (display_offset)",
  "unity": "(x, y, z) -> Unity (-x, z, -y); the front (-y) is the prefab's +Z",
  "states": "ground: TrashPile_<Kind> lies on the ground; picked up -> the pile is hidden / removed and TrashClump_<Kind> is in the hands (Hand_Grip at the hand); put down / dropped -> the clump goes and the pile is placed where it lands (origin on the ground, any yaw)",
  "colliders": "BoxCollider per model: the pile - its bounds (low box over the heap), the clump - the bale",
  "materials": "M_Trash_Trash: one baked PSX atlas, point filter (the piles ~64 px/m, the clumps in the hands twice that)",
